---
/**
 * Act II, section 05: error tracking, and the Autofix beat.
 *
 * The copy describes what the surface shows and stops there. Autofix is stated as the context it
 * assembles — the grouped error, the stack trace, the release, the repository — rather than as a
 * promise about what comes back, because the honest claim is the one about the context.
 */
import { IssuesInbox } from '../../surfaces/IssuesInbox/IssuesInbox';
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---

<section class="b-band" id="s05" data-act="1">
  <div class="b-shell">
    <SectionHead act="1" index="05" kicker="Console · error tracking">
      <Fragment slot="title">When it breaks, you get the frame that threw it.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="lede">
        Errors are grouped across every runtime in the stage, counted, and pinned to the release they appeared in. The
        detail pane carries the stack trace with your own source frames marked. <b>Autofix with Claude</b> hands all of
        that — the grouped error, the trace, the release, the repository it came from — to Claude in one step,
        instead of making you assemble it from four tabs.
      </Fragment>
    </SectionHead>

    <figure class="b-figure b-reveal">
      <div class="b-figure__stage site-panel">
        <IssuesInbox />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="b-figure__caption">
        <b>Two open issues on production.</b> The occurrences sparkline is the same burst the metrics above show, an
        hour wide.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
